<title>GREECE: GREEK MAY BUILDING MATERIALS PRICE INDEX UP 6.6PCT.</title>
<headline>GREEK MAY BUILDING MATERIALS PRICE INDEX UP 6.6PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's building materials price</p>
<p>index for new housing rose 6.6 percent year-on-year in May from</p>
<p>7.5 percent in May 1996, the National Statistics Service (NSS)</p>
<p>said in a statement.</p>
<p>The index was up an average 6.7 percent year-on-year in the</p>
<p>period January-May 1997 compared to 7.6 percent and 7.4 percent</p>
<p>in the same period in 1996 and 1995.</p>
<p>					May 97    April 97    May 96</p>
<p>    Month/month change (pct)    0.6	 ---	   0.5</p>
<p>    Year-on-year (pct)	    6.6	 ---	   7.5</p>
<p>    Index (1990=100)	    196.6	195.5	 184.4</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
